cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Uncertainty-gated selection for block-sparse attention"
abstract: >-
  A value-of-information router for block-sparse attention selectors:
  measures the normalised cutoff margin per query-tile and expands the
  attended set for the most uncertain tiles. Backbone-agnostic; composes
  with SSA-style mean pooling and Quest's K-min/K-max upper bound to
  reach within 2 pp of dense on RULER NIAH-multikey and lift LongBench-v2
  medium paired recall from 0.40 to 0.75 at fixed budget.
